!!! Configuration, and the sites a server answers for.
!!!
!!! A server configured only by environment variables is a server nobody can
!!! review: there is no file to put in version control, no way to describe two
!!! sites, and no record of what the running process was told. This reads a
!!! nildata file.
!!!
!!! nildata rather than JSON or a format of our own, because it is the
!!! framework's own: `nil.project.nildata` describes a build, so
!!! `nil.web.nildata` describing a server needs no new parser, no new tooling
!!! and nothing to learn.
!!!
!!! Everything has a default and a missing file is not an error. A server that
!!! will not start without a config file is one that cannot be tried out, and
!!! the defaults here are the ones a developer wants: loopback, port 8080, one
!!! site, no logs.
!!!
!!! Every nildata call here spells its first argument `` `value` ``. That is
!!! not a style choice: the Ny declaration names the parameter `value`, which
!!! is a Matrix keyword, so a backtick escape is the only way to call it by
!!! name. Worth knowing before writing the next one.

book nilweb.config.settings

read nil.std.core
read nil.std.io.file
read nil.std.nildata
read nil.std.text
read nil.std.text.string_utils
read everything from nilweb.text.scan


!!! One site: which Host it answers for, and where its files are.
!!!
!!! A `host` of "" is the default site, used when no other matches. Without
!!! one, a request for an unknown Host is refused — which is the right answer
!!! for a server with several sites on one address, and the wrong one for a
!!! server with a single site reached by IP as well as by name.

public site begin record
    field host as text
    field template-root as text
    field public-root as text
    !!! Served for a request whose path names a directory. Empty means no
    !!! directory index: a request for "/" then has to be a route.
    field index-page as text
end record


public settings begin record
    field host as text
    field port as number
    field connection-limit as number
    field access-log as text
    field error-log as text
    field share-port as boolean
    field reload-templates as boolean
    field sites as array of site
    !!! False when a file was named and could not be read or parsed. The
    !!! defaults are still filled in, so a caller may serve anyway — but it
    !!! should say what it ignored first.
    field loaded as boolean
    field complaint as text
end record


public default-settings returns settings begin paragraph
    variable sites as array of site is []
    append build site with host being "", template-root being "web",
        public-root being "web/public", index-page being "" to sites
    give build settings with
        host being "127.0.0.1",
        port being 8080,
        connection-limit being 1024,
        access-log being "",
        error-log being "",
        share-port being false,
        reload-templates being false,
        sites being sites,
        loaded being true,
        complaint being ""
end paragraph


!!! --- Read a configuration file.
!!!
!!! An absent file gives the defaults and `loaded` true: not naming a file and
!!! naming one that is not there are the same intention, and neither is a
!!! failure. A file that is there and will not parse is a failure, because
!!! somebody wrote it and meant something by it.

public load-settings receives path as text returns settings begin paragraph
    when path equals "" then
        give default-settings with nothing
    end when
    when not (nil.std.io::exists with path being path) then
        give default-settings with nothing
    end when
    value loaded is nil.std.io::read_text with path being path
    consider loaded
        when Result.Ok holding source then give settings-from with source being source
        when Result.Error holding why then give refused with complaint being "could not read " plus path plus ": " plus why
        otherwise give refused with complaint being "could not read " plus path
    end consider
end paragraph


refused receives complaint as text returns settings begin paragraph
    value base is default-settings with nothing
    give build settings with
        host being base.host, port being base.port, connection-limit being base.connection-limit,
        access-log being base.access-log, error-log being base.error-log,
        share-port being base.share-port, reload-templates being base.reload-templates,
        sites being base.sites, loaded being false, complaint being complaint
end paragraph


!!! --- Parse configuration from nildata text.

public settings-from receives source as text returns settings begin paragraph
    value base is default-settings with nothing
    value parsed is nil.std.nildata::loads with source being source
    consider parsed
        when Result.Error holding why then give refused with complaint being "the configuration did not parse: " plus why
        when Result.Ok holding root then begin block
            value stated-schema is text-at with holder being root, key being "schema", fallback being ""
            when not (stated-schema equals "") and not (stated-schema equals "nil.web.v1") then
                !!! Refused rather than read on a best-effort basis. A file
                !!! declaring a schema this does not know may mean something
                !!! different by the same key names, and guessing is how a
                !!! server ends up listening somewhere nobody asked for.
                give refused with complaint being "unknown configuration schema: " plus stated-schema
            end when
            give build settings with
                host being (text-at with holder being root, key being "host", fallback being base.host),
                port being (number-at with holder being root, key being "port", fallback being base.port),
                connection-limit being (number-at with holder being root, key being "connectionLimit",
                    fallback being base.connection-limit),
                access-log being (text-at with holder being root, key being "accessLog", fallback being ""),
                error-log being (text-at with holder being root, key being "errorLog", fallback being ""),
                share-port being (flag-at with holder being root, key being "sharePort", fallback being false),
                reload-templates being (flag-at with holder being root, key being "reloadTemplates", fallback being false),
                sites being (sites-in with root being root, fallback being base.sites),
                loaded being true,
                complaint being ""
        end block
        otherwise give refused with complaint being "the configuration did not parse"
    end consider
end paragraph


!!! --- The sites array, or one default site when it is absent or empty.

sites-in receives root as nil.std.nildata.Value, fallback as array of site returns array of site begin paragraph
    value found is nil.std.nildata::object_get with `value` being root, key being "sites"
    consider found
        when Result.Ok holding maybe then begin block
            consider maybe
                when Option.Some holding listed then give sites-of with listed being listed, fallback being fallback
                otherwise give fallback
            end consider
        end block
        otherwise give fallback
    end consider
end paragraph


sites-of receives listed as nil.std.nildata.Value, fallback as array of site returns array of site begin paragraph
    value counted is nil.std.nildata::size with `value` being listed
    variable total as number is 0
    consider counted
        when Result.Ok holding amount then set total to amount
        otherwise set total to 0
    end consider
    when total is at most 0 then
        give fallback
    end when

    variable out as array of site is []
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than total
        value item is nil.std.nildata::array_get with `value` being listed, index being index
        consider item
            when Result.Ok holding maybe then begin block
                consider maybe
                    when Option.Some holding held then
                        append (site-of with holder being held) to out
                    otherwise say ""
                end consider
            end block
            otherwise say ""
        end consider
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    when (the length of out) equals 0 then
        give fallback
    end when
    give out
end paragraph


site-of receives holder as nil.std.nildata.Value returns site begin paragraph
    value templates is text-at with holder being holder, key being "templateRoot", fallback being "web"
    give build site with
        host being (nil.std.text::to_lower with s being
            (text-at with holder being holder, key being "host", fallback being "")),
        template-root being templates,
        public-root being (text-at with holder being holder, key being "publicRoot",
            fallback being templates plus "/public"),
        index-page being (text-at with holder being holder, key being "indexPage", fallback being "")
end paragraph


!!! --- The site that answers for a Host header.
!!!
!!! The port is stripped, because "example.com" and "example.com:8080" are the
!!! same site, and the comparison folds case because a host name is
!!! case-insensitive. An IPv6 literal in brackets is compared whole.
!!!
!!! No wildcard matching. "*.example.com" looks helpful and is the shape that
!!! ends up serving one tenant's files to another when a subdomain is added
!!! and nobody re-reads the config; a site that wants several names lists them.

public site-for receives held-settings as settings, host-header as text returns site begin paragraph
    value wanted is host-only with header being host-header
    repeat for each one in held-settings.sites
        when not (one.host equals "") and one.host equals wanted then
            give one
        end when
    end repeat
    repeat for each one in held-settings.sites
        when one.host equals "" then
            give one
        end when
    end repeat
    !!! No match and no default. The caller answers 404 rather than serving
    !!! some other tenant's site, which is the whole point of the check.
    give build site with host being "", template-root being "", public-root being "", index-page being ""
end paragraph


public has-site receives held-settings as settings, host-header as text returns boolean begin paragraph
    value chosen is site-for with held-settings being held-settings, host-header being host-header
    give not (chosen.template-root equals "")
end paragraph


!!! --- The host part of a Host header, folded, without its port.

public host-only receives header as text returns text begin paragraph
    value trimmed is nil.std.text::trim with s being header
    when trimmed equals "" then
        give ""
    end when
    !!! An IPv6 literal is "[::1]:8080"; the brackets have to survive and the
    !!! colons inside them must not be mistaken for the port separator.
    when nil.std.text::starts_with with s being trimmed, prefix being "[" then
        value closing is nil.std.text::index_of with s being trimmed, needle being "]"
        when closing is less than 0 then
            give nil.std.text::to_lower with s being trimmed
        end when
        give nil.std.text::to_lower with s being
            (nil.std.text::substring with s being trimmed, start being 0, length being closing plus 1)
    end when
    give nil.std.text::to_lower with s being (before-first with input being trimmed, separator being ":")
end paragraph


!!! --- nildata accessors, each giving a fallback rather than a Result.
!!!
!!! Configuration reading is the one place where a missing key is ordinary and
!!! a wrong type is close to it, and threading a Result through every field
!!! would make the settings record above unreadable. A malformed value takes
!!! the default; a malformed *file* was already refused above.

text-at receives holder as nil.std.nildata.Value, key as text, fallback as text returns text begin paragraph
    value found is nil.std.nildata::object_get with `value` being holder, key being key
    consider found
        when Result.Ok holding maybe then begin block
            consider maybe
                when Option.Some holding held then begin block
                    value shown is nil.std.nildata::text_value with `value` being held
                    consider shown
                        when Result.Ok holding out then give out
                        otherwise give fallback
                    end consider
                end block
                otherwise give fallback
            end consider
        end block
        otherwise give fallback
    end consider
end paragraph


number-at receives holder as nil.std.nildata.Value, key as text, fallback as number returns number begin paragraph
    value found is nil.std.nildata::object_get with `value` being holder, key being key
    consider found
        when Result.Ok holding maybe then begin block
            consider maybe
                when Option.Some holding held then begin block
                    value amount is nil.std.nildata::as_i64 with `value` being held
                    consider amount
                        when Result.Ok holding out then give out
                        otherwise give fallback
                    end consider
                end block
                otherwise give fallback
            end consider
        end block
        otherwise give fallback
    end consider
end paragraph


flag-at receives holder as nil.std.nildata.Value, key as text, fallback as boolean returns boolean begin paragraph
    value found is nil.std.nildata::object_get with `value` being holder, key being key
    consider found
        when Result.Ok holding maybe then begin block
            consider maybe
                when Option.Some holding held then begin block
                    value held-flag is nil.std.nildata::bool_value with `value` being held
                    consider held-flag
                        when Result.Ok holding out then give out
                        otherwise give fallback
                    end consider
                end block
                otherwise give fallback
            end consider
        end block
        otherwise give fallback
    end consider
end paragraph
